GXEMUL-SEC/tools/pipeline/ledger.json-17812-     "d": "✓",
GXEMUL-SEC/tools/pipeline/ledger.json-17813-     "date": "2026-08-23",
GXEMUL-SEC/tools/pipeline/ledger.json-17814-     "note": "[filed by the MAIN LOOP wearing the fable5 model -- seat and adjudicator are distinct hats; the seats that found it are named in the text] COVERAGE DEBT from #458, filed under #447's precedent: hypothetical edits in uncovered product cells against a detector measured ABOVE the vacuity floor. FIVE SEATS found the class independently. Eight shapes: drop SH_INTEVT_HUDI (0x600); drop SH_INTEVT_GPIOI (0x620); drop RTC_PRI/RTC_CUI (0x4a0/0x4c0 -- only ATI is read); drop the REF pair (0x580/0x5a0); drop the DMAC loop (0x640-0x6c0); drop the SCI loop (0x4e0-0x540); `i<=SH_INTEVT_SCI_TEI` -> `i<` (drops 0x540 alone); and a wrong-DESTINATION variant that TRANSPOSES the GPIO and H-UDI nibbles. Root cause is structural: none of those sources has an INTERRUPT_ASSERT in this tree, so no behavioural row can reach them. TWO FIXES, cheapest first: (a) one table-driven row writing each IPR to a distinct pattern and checking EVERY slot Table 19.6 assigns -- subsumes all eight; (b) a debugger interrupt-inject command (INTERRUPT_ASSERT by name on machine[0].cpu[0].irq[0x560], already registered at cpu_sh.c:210-223), which promotes them from table reads to real delivery rows and does not rot. Also file: the DMAC loop stops at DMAE and omits DMTE4-7 (H'780-H'7E0, also IPRC[11:8]), which exist on the SH7751R landisk runs."
GXEMUL-SEC/tools/pipeline/ledger.json-17815-    }
GXEMUL-SEC/tools/pipeline/ledger.json-17816-   ]
