GXEMUL-SEC/tools/pipeline/ledger.json-17835-     "date": "2026-08-23",
GXEMUL-SEC/tools/pipeline/ledger.json-17836-     "note": "PREDICTED, NOT MEASURED -- the seat said so itself. Mutant: guard #458's new rescan as `if (cpu->cd.sh.int_to_assert == 0) sh_recalc_int_to_assert(cpu);`. It escapes because `raise` asserts at priority 0 so the guard still fires; `lower` writes both IPR values BEFORE asserting, so nothing is standing during either store; and `deassert` uses the other path entirely. Guest-visible miss: assert SCIF at 15, then IPRC[7:4] := 1 with IMASK=1 -- hardware must drop it, the mutant keeps a stale level 15. THE KILL ROW IS ONE LINE: `run_deliver(0x00f0, 1, raise_iprc(0x0010))` wanting `refused`. NOTE this is a DETECTOR gap, not a code defect: the shipped code calls the rescan unconditionally and handles standing-lower correctly."
GXEMUL-SEC/tools/pipeline/ledger.json-17837-    }
GXEMUL-SEC/tools/pipeline/ledger.json-17838-   ]
