GXEMUL-SEC/tools/pipeline/ledger.json-17952-     "d": "✓",
GXEMUL-SEC/tools/pipeline/ledger.json-17953-     "date": "2026-08-23",
GXEMUL-SEC/tools/pipeline/ledger.json-17954-     "note": "doc/TODO.html:322-323 lists 'SH3-specific devices: Pretty much everything!' immediately followed by 'NetBSD/evbsh3, hpcsh!', grouping hpcsh with an SH3 target; machine_hpcsh.c:89 names SH7750, which is arch 4. TWO SEATS INDEPENDENTLY REFUSED TO SETTLE THIS FROM MEMORY, which is the #357/#362/#365 citation failure NOT repeating -- there is no SH-3 manual in _scratchpad, hpcsh's platid/bootinfo block is entirely commented out, HISTORY never mentions hpcsh, and vripreg.h (included by machine_hpcsh.c) is NEC VR41xx MIPS, a copy-paste leftover from hpcmips. IF IT IS SETTLED as SH-3, note what changes: arch-3 removes the WHOLE dev_sh4 block (CCN/MMU, INTC, TMU, RTC, BSC, DMAC, SCIF, TLB arrays, PCIC), both SH-3 interrupt handlers are /* TODO */ stubs (cpu_sh.c:527-533) that silently drop asserts, and cpu_sh.c:224 uses a leftover UTLB loop counter as templ.line -- latent today only because that handler is a stub. Obtain a source first; the SH7750 precedent shows that costs one download."
GXEMUL-SEC/tools/pipeline/ledger.json-17955-    }
