GXEMUL-SEC/tools/pipeline/ledger.json-19661-     "note": "*** BOTH ROWS PASS THE REGRESS PHASE.  Records-only review -- read, grep and diff; nothing built, nothing run, deliberately, because a measuring seat was live on this machine and a pty-driven instrument corrupts silently under load. ***  **gdrompionull**: 13 rows = 5 controls + 8 detector rows, and **no row expects `exit1`** -- the load-bearing fact under the round-2 de-fatalisations.  Gate-wired, denominator pinned to a literal, per-row presence checks all padded-column safe.  **Every score resolves to a log**, and the ORACLE-CORRECTION ORDER IS PRESERVED ON DISK rather than asserted: `prefix_HEAD_13of13.raw` (old pin), `repin_HEAD_RED.raw` (12/13, the committed build measured RED under the new expectations), then `postfix_465*.raw`.  The `Md_nolen` kill is exactly as claimed (10/13 and 7/9 against 13/13 and 9/9 bases).  **gdromexitsix**: it CHECKED the exit census rather than accepting it and reproduced it independently -- 18 occurrences, 3 live, `:792` a false positive, `:1055` unreachable, `:1094`/`:1154` belonging to `gdromcondlies`.  All six filed sites disposed; closure strands no live site.  Its `gdrom_decline_probe.py` gate section and `r2measure_20260829` logs match the witness field byte-for-byte, with `R2MEASURE_DONE` as tail-1."
GXEMUL-SEC/tools/pipeline/ledger.json-19662-    }
