GXEMUL-SEC/tools/pipeline/ledger.json-20524-     "note": "PANEL panel_20260824_055023. *** FOUND A REAL ESCAPE, AND IT SAT UNREAD FOR HOURS BECAUSE I RECORDED ITS VERDICT LINE AND NEVER OPENED THE 6,732 BYTES BEHIND IT. *** The mutant: in the `d->data == NULL` arm, move `idata = 0` INSIDE the `if (!(d->warned & GDROM_W_DMANODATA))` block -- what a maintainer tidying that block, or believing 'ack the start only when we actually complain', would write. The FIRST no-data trigger still prints and still clears; every later one leaves the guest's trigger value in dma_reg[6] and +0x18 reads BUSY FOREVER. THE SEAT NAMED WHY NO ROW CATCHES IT, EXACTLY: 'That is the exact shape `arm twice` was written to close. The row is arming-only. There is no `nodata twice`.' VERIFIED by parsing every session in the probe: the sessions reaching the NO-DATA arm each trigger it ONCE (their second +0x18 reference is the readback, not a second trigger), and `both decl` drives each arm once rather than one arm twice. Under the CORRECTED clause (d) -- which enumerates predicates the fix DEPENDS ON, not only those it adds -- this is guard-kept-repair-nulled, an L2 floor breach. THE GATE'S WARNING WAS LITERAL: 'a seat that answered and was not recorded is an UNREAD REVIEW, and this project has twice found real defects sitting in one.' This is the third."
GXEMUL-SEC/tools/pipeline/ledger.json-20525-    },
