GXEMUL-SEC/tools/pipeline/ledger.json-23325-   "state_note": "FILED 2026-08-28 BY OWNER DECISION, from the round that fixed `asanunbuildable`.\n\n**THE GAP:** `precommit_check.sh` enforces build-asan propagation for `$CHANGED` -- the files\nTHIS commit touches.  That bound is deliberate and correct; its own comment says *a gate that\nhard-fails on a tree someone chose not to build is a gate that gets switched off*.  **But a\nfile no round happens to touch is never checked**, so a tree that was already stale when the\n2026-08-27 ruling landed stays stale forever.  Measured: 111 divergent .c/.h files, of which\n`diskimage.h` and `makeautodev.sh` broke the build -- neither touched by a recent round.\n\n**THE SHAPE, worth stating because it generalises past this tree: an INCREMENTAL sync check\ncannot detect a stale BASELINE.**  The tree passed every commit while compiling nothing.\n\n*** THE DECISION: a SOFT-WARNING full `diff -rq` over the .c/.h set, SKIPPED ENTIRELY when the\ntree is absent. ***  Warn, do not hard-fail -- and skip on absence -- so the\nabsence-is-not-a-failure property that keeps this gate switched on is preserved.  Chosen over\na hard fail (which is the exact shape the gate's author warned gets disabled) and over doing\nnothing (which leaves the next drift to be found the way this one was: by someone trying to\nuse the tree).\n\n**TWO NEGATIVE CONTROLS ARE OWED, as for any gate change:** (1) with a source file deliberately\nreverted in build-asan/, the check WARNS and names it; (2) with the tree absent entirely, the\ncheck is SILENT and the gate stays green.  Ships as its own small harness round -- a gate edit\nmust not ride in on a diff reviewed for something else.\n\nSCOPE NOTE: `Makefile`s legitimately differ (they carry the ASan COPTIM) and must be excluded;\nthe measured expectation after a correct sync is **14 differing files, all Makefiles, zero\nothers**.  `est/` is NOT in scope -- it has a declared divergence allowlist\n(`tools/est_divergence.txt`); build-asan has none, which is why any .c/.h divergence there is\nstaleness by definition."
GXEMUL-SEC/tools/pipeline/ledger.json-23326-  },
GXEMUL-SEC/tools/pipeline/ledger.json-23327-  {
