8114: ### `sh4iprunpinned` �?" open (coverage debt from #458)
8115: 
8116: *** FIVE SEATS INDEPENDENTLY FOUND THE SAME ESCAPE CLASS, AND IT IS A REAL LIMIT ON WHAT
8117: `sh_iprbcd_probe.py` CAN SEE. *** Filed, not fixed: `#447`'s precedent governs �?" these are
8118: hypothetical edits in uncovered product cells against a detector measured ABOVE the vacuity
8119: floor, which is coverage debt, and the round's ask-again is capped at one finding.
8120: 
8121: `#458` maps every Table 19.6 source, but only three slots are ever READ by a row �?"
8122: `iprio_560` (WDT), `iprio_480` (RTC ATI) and, from the ask-again, `iprio_240` (IRQ2/IRL0).
8123: Delete any single mapping line for a slot no row reads and the detector scores full marks:
8124: 
8125: | escape | what it leaves wrong | named by |
8126: |---|---|---|
8127: | drop `SH_INTEVT_HUDI` | H-UDI (`0x600`) stuck at 0 | grok, glm |
8128: | drop `SH_INTEVT_GPIOI` | GPIO (`0x620`) stuck at 0 | deepseek, agy |
8129: | drop `RTC_PRI` / `RTC_CUI` | `0x4a0`/`0x4c0` stuck at 0; `ipra rtc` reads only ATI | minimax, agy |
8130: | drop the `REF` pair | `0x580`/`0x5a0` stuck at 0; `iprb wdt` reads only WDT | agy |
8131: | drop the DMAC loop | DMTE0..DMAE (`0x640`-`0x6c0`) all 0 | minimax |
8132: | drop the SCI loop | SCI ERI/RXI/TXI/TEI (`0x4e0`-`0x540`) all 0 | minimax, codex |
8133: | `i<=SH_INTEVT_SCI_TEI` -> `i<` | SCI TEI (`0x540`) alone | codex |
8134: | map only `SCIF_TXI` | ERI/RXI/BRI untested; the probe drives TXI only | grok |
8135: 
8136: **The root cause is structural, not sloppiness.** None of those sources has an
8137: `INTERRUPT_ASSERT` anywhere in this tree, so no behavioural row can reach them; and the
8138: probe reads the table only where a row was written to. The general fix is one of:
8139: 
8140: * a **table-driven row** that writes each IPR to a distinct pattern and checks EVERY slot
8141:   Table 19.6 assigns �?" one session, ~30 reads, and it subsumes every line above; or
8142: * a debugger **interrupt-inject** command (`INTERRUPT_ASSERT` by name on
8143:   `machine[0].cpu[0].irq[0x560]`, which `cpu_sh.c:210-223` already registers), which would
8144:   promote these from table reads to real delivery rows. **grok notes this makes the probe's
8145:   "no behavioural test can ever replace these" claim too strong** �?" it is true only of the
8146:   Python probe as it stands, because no such command exists today.
8147: 
8148: The first is cheap and should come first. The second is the one that does not rot.
