455: 	 *
456: 	 *  It sets per-pin IRL priorities in IRLM=1 mode -- Table 19.4 at :39965,
457: 	 *  "SH7750 IRL3-IRL0 Pins and Interrupt Levels (When IRLM = 1)" -- which
458: 	 *  dev_sh4.c:2386-2388 REFUSES outright ("ICR IRLM bit 0x%04x not
459: 	 *  implemented -- write ignored"), so it can never be in effect.  And its four nibbles ALIAS live slots: IRL0-3 are
460: 	 *  0x240/0x2a0/0x300/0x360, which are also IRQ2/IRQ5/IRQ8/IRQ11 -- owned by
461: 	 *  the hardwired 15..1 loop above and used today by the PCIC lines and the
462: 	 *  dreamcast ASIC.
463: 	 *
464: 	 *  Measured: one guest `IPRD := 0` -- the exact store OpenBSD/landisk 7.6
465: 	 *  makes during boot -- drops those four slots from 0xd/0xa/0x7/0x4 to ZERO,
466: 	 *  masking four PCIC lines permanently, while a control slot not in IPRD
467: 	 *  (IRQ10, the wdc) is untouched.  A variant reading IPRD scored the same as
468: 	 *  this one -- 10/10, measured when the detector had ten rows -- so reading
469: 	 *  it buys nothing and costs that.
470: 	 *
471: 	 *  TWO STRONGER FACTS THAN THE ONES THIS COMMENT FIRST GAVE, both supplied by
472: 	 *  the pass-2 panel and both re-read here before use:
473: 	 *
474: 	 *  (a0) THE STRONGEST ARM, and the one an earlier draft left out: :39956-39959
475: 	 *      says that when independent interrupt requests are used, "in the SH7750
476: 	 *      the interrupt priority levels are FIXED (table 19.4)", and only "in the
477: 	 *      SH7750S or SH7750R" can they "be set in interrupt priority register D".
478: 	 *      So on plain SH7750 -- one of the four types in SH_CPU_TYPE_DEFS -- IPRD
479: 	 *      controls nothing EVEN IN IRLM=1.  The IRLM refusal below is the weaker
480: 	 *      arm; it covers SH7750R/SH7751R, while this covers SH7750 outright.
481: 	 *  (a) IPRD IS SH7750S/SH7750R ONLY -- Rev.7.00 note 3 at :39881, repeated at
482: 	 *      :40248.  machine_dreamcast.c:165 asks for "SH7750", on which the
483: 	 *      register does not exist at all, so reading it would invent one.
484: 	 *      machine_landisk.c:125 asks for "SH7751R", which does have it.
485: 	 *  (b) The disease is NON-CONFORMANCE, not the masking.  In IRLM=0 the
486: 	 *      hardware IGNORES IPRD outright, so consulting it would be wrong even
487: 	 *      if no line were masked; the four dead PCIC lines are the symptom.
488: 	 *
489: 	 *  And a third, weaker one -- suggestive, NOT load-bearing, and recorded that
490: 	 *  way because a panel seat objected to it carrying weight:
491: 	 *  IPRA-IPRC reset to H'0000 but *** IPRD resets to H'DA74 ***, stated three
492: 	 *  times independently (:39856, :40194, :48567).  Those nibbles are
493: 	 *  13/10/7/4, and the hardwired loop above hands IRQ2/IRQ5/IRQ8/IRQ11 -- the
494: 	 *  slots IRL0-3 alias -- exactly 13/10/7/4.  The model already sits on the
495: 	 *  hardware's IPRD reset state, nibble for nibble, so reading IPRD could not
496: 	 *  improve the reset case even in principle; it could only let a guest write
497: 	 *  move the model AWAY from a correct default, which is what the measured
498: 	 *  `IPRD := 0` does.  Whether upstream chose that ramp for this reason or it
499: 	 *  fell out is not determinable from the code.
500: 	 */
